# ── ECC install-target output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Running a project-scoped target (`kodelythecc --target cursor-project` et al)
# inside this repo writes its whole payload here. In 2.19.0 that swept 2,570
# duplicate files into the package — 5 MB became 21 MB. These are build output,
# never sources. The `files` allowlist in package.json is the real guard; this
# keeps them out of git as well.
.agent/
.agents
.aider-ecc/
.clinerules/
.cursor/
.gemini/
